comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T20:58:39.011Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence for the registry-not-prose acceptance criterion: scripts/release/gate-registry.mjs discovers the gate inventory by regex over GitHub workflow step NAMES — GATE_STEP_PATTERN matches /\\b(build|typecheck|test|gates?|check|scan|analysis|benchmark|verify|dogfood|release pipeline|enforce|coverage|quality)\\b/i and NON_GATE_STEP_PATTERN excludes steps beginning setup|install|checkout|download|upload|restore|record|resolve|alert|create github release. A gate's identity is therefore its human-written title, so renaming a step silently changes the inventory and adding a gate whose step name avoids the vocabulary makes it invisible to its own ownership registry. Same failure shape as pm-dqtzva (release gate classifying production errors by message prose) on a different surface: enforcement reading prose rather than a declared contract."
body: ""
